For the recycle calculation, each pass converts \(15.0\%\) of the remaining \(\mathrm{N_2}\), so the fraction remaining after one pass is \(q=0.85\).

For the annual production of \(660{,}000\ \text{t NH}_3\) at \(97\%\) overall yield, the fresh \(\mathrm{N_2}\) feed is:

\[
n_{\mathrm{N_2,feed}}
=
\frac{660000\times 10^6\ \text{g}}{17.03\ \text{g mol}^{-1}}
\times \frac{1}{2}
\times \frac{1}{0.97}
\approx 2.00\times 10^{10}\ \text{mol}
\]

After 58 cycles:

\[
n_{\mathrm{N_2,rem}}
=
2.00\times 10^{10}\ \text{mol}
\times 0.85^{58}
\]

\[
0.85^{58} \approx 8.05\times 10^{-5}
\]

\[
n_{\mathrm{N_2,rem}} \approx 1.61\times 10^6\ \text{mol}
\]

\[
m_{\mathrm{N_2,rem}}
=
1.61\times 10^6\ \text{mol}
\times 28.01\ \text{g mol}^{-1}
\approx 4.51\times 10^7\ \text{g}
\approx 45.0\ \text{t}
\]

For the overall yield to reach \(97.0\%\):

\[
1-0.85^{n+1}=0.97
\]

\[
0.85^{n+1}=0.03
\]

\[
n+1=\frac{\ln 0.03}{\ln 0.85}=21.6
\]

Thus \(n=20.6\), so \(21\) additional recycle cycles are needed after the first pass, corresponding to \(22\) total passes through the reactor.

FINAL ANSWER: \(m(\mathrm{N_2})_{\text{remaining after 58 cycles}} \approx 45.0\ \text{t}\); \(n=21\) additional recycle cycles (\(22\) total passes).

